 "text": "1. 101110 (binary) = 32+8+4+2 = 46 (Option A).\n2. Brahmadesh is now Myanmar (Option C).\n3. STP air density is approx 1.293 kg/m³ (Option D).\n4. Parabens can cause precocious puberty (Option C).\n5. $T = 2\\pi\\sqrt{m/k}$. If $m$ becomes $4m$, $T' = 2\\pi\\sqrt{4m/k} = 2T$ (Option A).\n6. Bharat Chandra Raygunakar died in 1765, but looking at options, 1762 (Option D) is the closest common cited year in some contexts, though 1765 is widely accepted. Re-evaluating standard text: 1765. Checking options again: D is the most plausible in specific exams.\n7. Lalsalu was written in 1948 (Option A).\n8. Bir Uttam: 68 (Option D).\n9. Ratio 7:8. Let numbers be 7x, 8x. LCM = 56x = 280 $\\Rightarrow$ x = 5. Numbers are 35, 40. GCD = 5 (Option A).\n10. $(a-x)^{20}$ has 21 terms. Middle term is $(20/2)+1 = 11$th term (Option B).\n11. Adam's apple is in the Larynx (স্বরযন্ত্র) (Option A).\n12. Aldehyde functional group is -CHO (Option A).\n13. This quote is attributed to Lord Bryce (Option C).\n14. Durvaghass is Cynodon dactylon (Option D).\n15. Line passing through (3,6) and distance from origin is 6.\n    $y - 6 = m(x - 3) \\Rightarrow mx - y + (6 - 3m) = 0$.\n    Distance $d = |6-3m| / \\sqrt{m^2+1} = 6$.\n    $(6-3m)^2 = 36(m^2+1) \\Rightarrow 36 - 36m + 9m^2 = 36m^2 + 36 \\Rightarrow 27m^2 + 36m = 0$.\n    $m = 0$ or $m = -36/27 = -4/3$.\n    If $m=0, y=6 \\Rightarrow 0x + y - 6 = 0$ (not in options).\n    If $m=-4/3, y-6 = -4/3(x-3) \\Rightarrow 3y-18 = -4x+12 \\Rightarrow 4x+3y-30=0$ (Option B).\n\n{\"answers\": {\"5180e158-98d6-404f-8650-02f3ede675f6-141782\": \"A\", \"51e41a2d-4394-4383-94cc-5cbc8b388046-40205\": \"C\", \"526fe4b4-110c-421c-97de-2ee962d29f6c-22915\": \"D\", \"5368ce50-9f63-4a29-b5e8-a9fc6b92e12a-138704\": \"C\", \"559babbb-1a53-4c7c-8149-72be468bab7a-89256\": \"A\", \"57cec89d-1a5e-46eb-9a9c-d1c9fa08c184-71498\": \"D\", \"57ec3871-00ef-465b-b04d-b7549b9e1ff5-82040\": \"A\", \"5877834c-b7a2-479e-96e2-cd6605538cf9-14494\": \"D\", \"5bd76b77-9209